     "text": "**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Washington Jones and Pham Clinic**\n\nPatient: Lisa Whitehead \nDOB: 08/19/1946 \nSex: F \nMRN: 724770\n\n**Encounters:**\n\n**2026-06-19** \nReason for Visit: Vitamin D deficiency \nBP: 141/79 \nWeight: 159 lbs\n\nMs. Lisa Whitehead, a 79-year-old female, presented to the clinic on June 19, 2026, for follow-up on her vitamin D deficiency. She reported adhering to her prescribed regimen of ergocalciferol 5O000 IU. Physical examination was largely unremarkable with normal findings on cardiovascular, respiratory, and abdominal examinations. The patient exhibited stable vital signs with a blood pressure of 141/79 and a weight of 159 lbs. Her current medications include alendronate 70 mg for osteopenia and ergocalciferol 50000 IU for D deficiency. She continues to vape daily, as previously reported.\n\n**2025-01-27** \nReason for Visit: Insomnia only \nBP: 150/86 \nWeight: 160 lbs\n\nOn January 27, 2025, Ms. Whitehead returned for management of her insomnia, which is currently controlled. She is taking zolpidem 5 mg and trazodone 50 mg as prescribed. Ms. Whitehead reported occasional minor sleep disturbances but overall improved sleep patterns. Her blood pressure was noted at 150/86, and her weight was 160 lbs. The physical exam was otherwise unremarkable.\n\n**2023-09-07** \nReason for Visit: Medication refill \nBP: 146/86 \nWeight: 145 lbs\n\nMs. Whitehead visited on September 7, 2023, for medication refills. Her osteopenia, managed with 70 mg, and vitamin D deficiency, treated with ergocalciferol 50000 IU, remain controlled. She also continues to take zolpidem 5 mg and trazodone 50 mg for insomnia. Her blood pressure was recorded at 146/86, and her weight was 145 lbs. She denied any major complaints and maintained a stable physical exam.\n\n**Assessment/Plan:**\n\n- **Insomnia only** - Controlled; medications: 5 mg, trazodone 50 mg\n- **Osteopenia** - Controlled; medications: alendronate 70 mg\n- **Vitamin D deficiency** - Controlled; medications: ergocalciferol 50000 IU\n\nMs. Whitehead’s overall health remains stable with her conditions well-managed through the prescribed medication regimen. She continues to use a vape daily, as previously documented. Follow-up visits are recommended to her ongoing treatments and overall health status.\n"
    }
